\f2\i \cf2 Mum, everyone\'92s life is a test run.
\f1\i0 \
\'93Ms Jacobson! Ms Jacobson!\'94\
Sarah turned. \'93Chip!\'94\
Chip came close and she leaned on his hulk, not sure his ankles would take the extra stress.\
\'93Did you feel the seismic activity?\'94 Chip asked her.\
So there had been a quake. Little Clinton had felt it coming on and had woken her early. Sarah nodded. \'93Yes.\'94\
\'93That idiot Stoat is running tests, possibly on his own. He\'92ll be short-staffed, for sure.\'94\
\'93You go on ahead,\'94 Sarah said and took a sharp breath. \'93I\'92ll catch up.\'94\
Chip hesitated, then nodded.\
Sarah was caught by a sharp pain that made her growl. She called out to Chip as he disappeared beyond the arc of the corridor. \'93Break his fingers and poke his eyes out if you have to.\'94
